<h2>1. Who these terms are between</h2>
<p>These terms apply between WFT — Websites for Tradies ("WFT", "we", "us") and you, the client. They apply from the moment you accept a quote or make a payment, whichever happens first.</p>
<p>Your written quote is part of these terms. Where the quote and this page disagree, <strong>the quote wins</strong> — it describes your specific build.</p>

<h2>2. What we build</h2>
<p>The WFT tradie website package is a done-for-you website of five or more pages, built specifically for a New Zealand trade business. Unless your quote says otherwise, it includes:</p>
<ul>
  <li>A mobile-first website, typically home, services, about, project gallery and contact pages.</li>
  <li>All copywriting, written by us from a kickoff interview with you.</li>
  <li>A local SEO foundation: suburb and service-area targeting, meta tags and structured data.</li>
  <li>Google Business Profile setup or optimisation.</li>
  <li>A .nz domain registered in your business's name.</li>
  <li>Hosting, SSL and security setup, including {{ site.hostingIncluded }}. From day {{ site.planStartsDay }}, hosting continues under the Get Found Plan (section 7). You are free to host the site elsewhere instead — you own it.</li>
  <li>The "First Jobs" launch checklist and Google review strategy.</li>
</ul>
<p>We build websites for trade businesses operating in New Zealand. We don't take on work outside that.</p>

<h2>3. Price and payment</h2>
<p>The standard price is <strong>{{ site.priceDisplay }}</strong>, a one-time flat fee. Founding clients — the first ten businesses we build for — pay <strong>{{ site.foundingPriceDisplay }}</strong>.</p>
<p>The price on your quote is the price you pay. We don't issue surprise invoices, and we don't charge for scope that was agreed at kickoff. If you ask for work beyond what was agreed, we'll quote it separately and you can say no.</p>
<p>Payment terms — including any deposit and when the balance falls due — are set out in your written quote and confirmed before we start work.</p>
<p>All prices are in New Zealand dollars.</p>

<h2>4. What we need from you</h2>
<p>The build only runs to seven days because your input is small and specific. To hold up your end you need to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Attend a kickoff call of about 30 minutes.</li>
  <li>Send us photos of your work, and any logo or branding you already have.</li>
  <li>Review and approve draft copy and the preview site <strong>within 5 working days</strong> of us sending it.</li>
  <li>Give us the access we need to any existing domain, hosting or Google Business Profile.</li>
  <li>Make sure you have the right to use everything you send us — photos, logos, testimonials and text.</li>
</ul>
<p>If you supply material you don't own the rights to, that's on you, and you agree to cover us for any claim that results.</p>

<h2>5. The 7-Day Launch Pledge</h2>
<div class="callout">
  <p>Your website will be live within <strong>7 working days</strong> of your kickoff call. If we miss that deadline without giving you at least 48 hours' notice, we credit <strong>NZ$200</strong> against your invoice.</p>
</div>
<p>The clock runs on working days, excluding weekends and New Zealand public holidays. It pauses while we're waiting on you — if we're waiting on your photos or your copy approval, those days don't count against us. That's the only fair way to run a fixed timeline.</p>

<h2>6. The Jobs In 90 Guarantee</h2>
<div class="callout">
  <p>If your website doesn't generate at least one genuine job enquiry within <strong>90 days</strong> of going live, we rebuild it from scratch free of charge and keep working until it does.</p>
</div>
<p>A "genuine job enquiry" means a real prospective customer contacting you about work through your website — a form submission, a tracked phone call, or an email from the site. Spam, bots, sales pitches and enquiries from people you already know don't count.</p>
<p>The guarantee applies where all of the following are true:</p>
<ul>
  <li>You provided photos and approved copy within 5 working days of each draft.</li>
  <li>You were on the Get Found Plan for the full 90-day period. A site nobody is actively managing can't be guaranteed to rank, so this one isn't negotiable.</li>
  <li>You asked at least three past customers for a Google review after launch.</li>
  <li>The site stayed live and unmodified by anyone other than us for the full 90 days.</li>
  <li>You didn't redirect, deindex or take down the site during the period.</li>
</ul>
<p>The remedy under this guarantee is a free rebuild and continued work — it is not a cash refund.</p>

<h2>7. The Get Found Plan</h2>
<p>The Get Found Plan is our ongoing service at <strong>{{ site.planPriceDisplay }}</strong>. It covers hosting, SSL, backups and security, monthly Google Business Profile management, ongoing local SEO, review generation, monthly reporting, and small site updates.</p>
<p>Your first month is included in the build price, and the plan starts from day {{ site.planStartsDay }}. There is <strong>no lock-in contract</strong> — you can cancel at any time with 30 days' notice, and we won't make it awkward.</p>
<p>If you cancel, you keep the website and the domain. You will need to arrange hosting elsewhere, and we will hand over your files to do it.</p>
<p>If you cancel, your Jobs In 90 Guarantee ends with it, for the reason given in section 6.</p>

<h2>8. Who owns what</h2>
<p>Once your invoice is paid in full:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>You own the website</strong> — the design, the copy we wrote for you, and the content. Outright.</li>
  <li><strong>You own the domain</strong> — it is registered in your business's name, not ours.</li>
  <li><strong>You can host it anywhere.</strong> If you leave, we hand over your files. We don't hold sites hostage.</li>
</ul>
<p>We keep ownership of the underlying tools, templates and systems we use to build sites — those aren't part of what you're buying. We'd also like to show your site in our portfolio and use it as an example of our work; tell us if you'd rather we didn't, and we won't.</p>
<p>Unless you ask us to remove it, we include a small "Website by WFT" credit in your site footer.</p>

<h2>9. Third-party services</h2>
<p>Your site relies on services we don't control — domain registrars, hosting providers, Google, and form processors. We choose reputable ones, but we're not responsible for their outages, price changes or policy decisions. If Google changes how ranking works, that's not a breach of these terms.</p>

<h2>10. Our liability</h2>
<p>We do this work properly and we stand behind it, which is why the guarantees above exist. Beyond those guarantees, our total liability for any claim relating to your build is limited to the amount you paid us.</p>
<p>We are not liable for indirect or consequential loss — lost profits, lost business opportunities, or loss of data.</p>
<p>Nothing in these terms limits any rights you have under the <strong>Consumer Guarantees Act 1993</strong> or the <strong>Fair Trading Act 1986</strong> where those Acts apply to you.</p>

<h2>11. Cancelling</h2>
<p>If you cancel after we've started, you pay for the work completed to that point. If we cancel — which we'd only do in unusual circumstances — we refund anything you've paid for work not yet done.</p>

<h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
<p>We may update these terms for future clients. The version that applies to you is the one in force when you accepted your quote. We won't change the deal on you mid-build.</p>

<h2>13. Governing law</h2>
<p>These terms are governed by New Zealand law, and the New Zealand courts have jurisdiction over any dispute. Before anyone goes near a court, we'll talk it through in good faith — that resolves almost everything.</p>

